<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-scalar-product-that-kills-the-second-coordinate> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "On the set of ordered pairs of real numbers with the usual addition but with a(x_1, x_2) = (a x_1, 0), Axiom 10 fails at x = (0, 1), because 1x = (0, 0) and not (0, 1). Axiom 6 fails at the same element in the form Apostol states it, since x + (-1)x = (0, 1) + (0, 0) = (0, 1) and not the zero element (0, 0); Axioms 1 through 5, 7, 8 and 9 all hold. Because the element y = (0, -1) does satisfy x + y = (0, 0), this structure satisfies the weakened Axiom 6' of Exercise 30(b) while still failing Axiom 10, and so it is a concrete model for the independence asserted there." .
