<http://studium.local/node/d%3A15-11-denominator-nonzero-by-positivity> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Passing from c_j (e_j, e_j) = (x, e_j) to formula (15.8) requires (e_j, e_j) nonzero. Apostol does not remark on it, but the justification is a two-link chain: a basis element cannot be O, since a set containing O is dependent; and a nonzero element has (e_j, e_j) > 0 by the positivity axiom. So (15.8) rests on strict positive definiteness even though no inequality appears in its statement." .
