<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-best-constant-is-the-mean-value> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "In Exercises 6 and 7 the approximating subspace is the one-dimensional space of constants, and the answers are (log 3)/2 for 1/x on (1, 3) and (e^2 - 1)/2 for e^x on (0, 2). Both are the average value of f over the interval, which is what the projection formula yields when the orthonormal basis of the subspace is the single normalized constant. Minimizing the integrated square error therefore gives the mean, not the midpoint between the maximum and minimum values of f." .
