<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aexponential-independence-proof-is-induction-on-n> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The architecture has three parts with a fixed dependency order: a base case n = 1 that needs nothing; an elimination step that picks the largest exponent a_M, normalizes by e^{-a_M x}, and takes x to +infinity to force c_M = 0; and a descent step that deletes the M-th term and calls the hypothesis on the remaining n - 1 functions. Only the elimination step uses the hypothesis that the exponents are distinct -- it is what makes a_k - a_M strictly negative for k not M -- while the recursion itself is independent of it, so the recursion depth equals the number of functions and each level kills exactly one coefficient." .
