<http://studium.local/node/d%3Ainner-product-symmetry-axiom> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Axiom (1): (x, y) = (y, x) for all x, y. What it forbids: any product that distinguishes the order of its arguments. Dropping only this axiom leaves a form linear in the second variable but with no transfer of that linearity to the first variable, so (x + y, z) can no longer be expanded, the expansion (x+y, x+y) = (x,x) + (y,y) + (x,y) + (y,x) used for the triangle inequality collapses, and the step 'pair the equation with x_1' in Theorems 15.10 and 15.11 becomes unavailable." .
