<http://studium.local/node/d%3Acauchy-schwarz-proof-inherited-from-theorem-12-3> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Apostol's proof strategy for 15.8 is a re-use argument, not a new computation. In proving the V_n case (Theorem 12.3) he was careful that the proof drew only on the properties of the dot product listed in Theorem 12.2, never on the component formula. Because those listed properties are precisely the inner-product axioms, the identical proof runs in any real Euclidean space. This is the paradigm of the whole section: axiomatize the properties actually used, and every theorem transfers for free." .
