<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aparseval-norm-form> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Setting x = y in (15.11) gives ||x||^2 = sum over i of |(x, e_i)|^2. Two collapses happen at once: (x, e_i) times its own conjugate becomes the squared modulus, and (x, x) becomes ||x||^2 by the definition of the norm. This is the abstract Pythagorean theorem, and specialized to the normalized trigonometric system it is the classical Parseval identity for Fourier coefficients." .
