<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aprojection-is-the-s-component-of-the-orthogonal-decomposition> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The formula defining the projection is the same formula that produced s in the existence proof of Theorem 15.15, so the projection of x on S is the S-component of x in the decomposition x = s + s perp. This identification is what lets Theorem 15.16 speak about the projection. Apostol never states this identification explicitly; it follows from the definition of the projection being verbatim formula (15.18) of the existence proof." .
