<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-log-weight-vanishing-at-an-endpoint> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 8 uses (f, g) = integral over [1, e] of (log x) f(x) g(x) dx. The weight log x is positive on the open interval but vanishes at the left endpoint x = 1, so it does not meet the letter of the requirement that the weight be a positive function on the closed interval. Positivity nevertheless survives, because a continuous f with a vanishing weighted integral of f^2 must be identically zero. The boundary case shows the positivity hypothesis on the weight is sufficient, not necessary." .
