<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-orthonormalizing-a-dependent-list-yields-a-shorter-basis> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The instruction is to orthonormalize the subspace spanned by the given vectors, and in each part the given list is dependent: in 1(a) x_3 = 2x_1 + x_2, in 1(b) x_3 lies in the plane of x_1 and x_2, in 2(a) x_1 - x_2 + x_3 - x_4 = O, and in 2(b) x_3 = 2x_1 - x_2. The Gram-Schmidt process returns O at the dependent step, so the resulting orthonormal basis has fewer elements than the input list. The exercises are a systematic drill in that detection, not in the arithmetic of independent input." .
