<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aaxiom-10-is-derivable-from-apostols-form-of-axiom-6> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Apostol does not remark on this; the derivation below is not in the text. Because Axiom 6 names (-1)x as a negative of x, Axiom 10 is not independent of the rest: Axiom 9 gives 1x + (-1)x = (1 + (-1))x = 0x, which is O by Theorem 15.3(a), while Axiom 6 gives x + (-1)x = O, so adding a negative of (-1)x to both relations yields 1x = x using only Axioms 3, 4, 5, 6 and 9. Under the more common existential form of the inverse axiom this derivation is unavailable and Axiom 10 is genuinely independent." .
