<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aadditivity-in-first-argument-derived> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "(x + y, z) = (x, z) + (y, z) is NOT one of Apostol's axioms. It follows by using symmetry (1) to swap into the second slot, applying additivity (2) there, and swapping back. This is the precise reason the symmetry axiom is load-bearing in the proofs: the expansion (x + y, x + y) = (x, x) + (y, y) + (x, y) + (y, x) that opens the proof of the triangle inequality, and the step 'pair the vanishing combination with x_1' in Theorem 15.10, both split a sum in the FIRST slot, which axiom (2) alone does not license." .
