<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-anisotropy-forces-a-definite-form> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 2 keeps symmetry, additivity and homogeneity but weakens axiom 4 to (4'): (x, x) = 0 if and only if x = O. The conclusion is that either (x, x) > 0 for every nonzero x or else (x, x) < 0 for every nonzero x. So the strict inequality in Apostol's axiom 4 is not an extra demand beyond nondegeneracy; up to an overall sign it is equivalent to it." .
