<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-legendre-family-changes-with-the-interval> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 4 orthonormalizes the powers t^n on (0, 1) and obtains 1, sqrt(3)(2t - 1), sqrt(5)(6t^2 - 6t + 1). The input sequence is the same one that produces the Legendre polynomials in 15.13, but there the interval is (-1, 1); changing the interval changes the whole orthogonal family. The Legendre polynomials are therefore not intrinsic to the powers, only to the powers together with an inner product." .
<http://studium.local/edge/1232> <http://studium.local/p/evQuote> "If real number is replaced by complex number in Axioms 2, 7, 8, and 9, the resulting structure is called a complex linear space." .
