<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Abest-approximation-in-a-finite-dimensional-subspace> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The approximation problem of the section: given x in a Euclidean space V and a finite-dimensional subspace S, find the element of S that minimizes the norm ||x - t|| over all t in S. 'Nearest' is measured by the norm induced by the inner product; that inner-product structure is not a precondition for stating the problem, which makes sense in any normed linear space, but it is what makes the projection the solution and makes the Pythagorean equality-condition argument available." .
