<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-metric-criteria-for-orthogonality> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "In a real Euclidean space, Exercises 3, 4 and 6 give conditions that mention only norms yet are equivalent to the vanishing of an inner product: (x, y) = 0 exactly when ||x + y|| = ||x - y||, and exactly when ||x + y||^2 = ||x||^2 + ||y||^2, while (x + y, x - y) = 0 exactly when ||x|| = ||y||. Orthogonality is therefore recoverable, in the real case, from the norm alone, which is the abstract form of the rhombus and Pythagoras pictures." .
