<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Ainner-product-axioms> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The four properties an inner product is required to satisfy for all x, y, z and all real scalars c: (1) (x,y) = (y,x) (commutativity, or symmetry); (2) (x, y+z) = (x,y) + (x,z) (distributivity, or linearity); (3) c(x,y) = (cx,y); and (x,x) > 0 if x is not the zero element. Apostol states these properties and regards them as axioms." .
