<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atheorem-15-16-approximation-theorem> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "If S is a finite-dimensional subspace of a Euclidean space V and x is in V, then the projection s of x on S satisfies ||x - s|| <= ||x - t|| for every t in S. Equality holds if and only if t = s, so the projection is the unique best approximation to x in S. The proof splits x - t = (x - s) + (s - t) into orthogonal parts and applies the Pythagorean formula." .
<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atheorem-15-4-subspace-criterion> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "THEOREM 15.4: if S is a nonempty subset of a linear space V, then S is a subspace if and only if S satisfies the closure axioms. The proof shows the remaining axioms are inherited from V or follow from closure." .
