<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Aweighted-integral-inner-product> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "On C(a, b) one may also define (f, g) as the integral of w(t)f(t)g(t) over [a, b], where w is a fixed positive function in C(a, b) called a weight function. The unweighted integral inner product is the case w(t) = 1 for all t." .
