<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atheorem-15-11-components-relative-to-an-orthogonal-basis> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "THEOREM 15.11: if V is a finite-dimensional Euclidean space of dimension n and S = {e_1, ..., e_n} is an orthogonal basis, then the components of x relative to the ordered basis are c_j = (x, e_j)/(e_j, e_j). In particular, for an orthonormal basis c_j = (x, e_j), so x is the sum of (x, e_i)e_i." .
