<http://studium.local/node/d%3Arescaling-preserves-orthogonality> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "If (y_i, y_j) = 0 for i != j then (c_i y_i, c_j y_j) = c_i conj(c_j) (y_i, y_j) = 0, by homogeneity in the first argument and conjugate homogeneity in the second, so any elementwise rescaling of an orthogonal set is again orthogonal. In a real Euclidean space the conjugate is absent and the factor is simply c_i c_j. Apostol uses this without comment whenever he normalizes, both in 15.11 and in 15.13." .
