<http://studium.local/node/x%3Aorthogonality-of-the-residual> <http://studium.local/p/divergence> "The logical direction is opposite. Apostol DEFINES s by a formula and then VERIFIES that x - s is orthogonal to each basis element, upgrading to all of S by linearity; orthogonality is a checked consequence. Strang IMPOSES orthogonality as the defining requirement -- the n right angles are the n equations -- and derives the formula from it; orthogonality is the input. Strang also names the residual twice over: as the error vector e = b - p, and as an element of N(A-transpose), the left nullspace. That second name is pure presentation artifact: it exists only because his subspace happens to be the column space of a matrix A, so 'orthogonal to S' can be rewritten as 'annihilated by A-transpose'. Apostol has no A, so he has one name where Strang has two, and Strang's second name is the one that connects the residual to his four-subspace picture." .
