<http://studium.local/node/d%3Atriangle-inequality-proof-bound-cross-terms-by-cauchy-schwarz> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Apostol applies the norm form of Cauchy-Schwarz to both cross terms, |(x, y)| <= ||x|| ||y|| and the same for the conjugate, obtaining ||x + y||^2 <= ||x||^2 + ||y||^2 + 2||x|| ||y|| = (||x|| + ||y||)^2, then takes square roots. This is the exact junction at which the triangle inequality depends on Cauchy-Schwarz: without the bound, the expansion of step 1 gives no inequality at all." .
