<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-normalizing-constant-breaks-at-the-index-zero> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "In Exercise 3 the normalized system is y_0 = 1/sqrt(pi) but y_n = sqrt(2/pi) cos nt for n >= 1, because the integral of 1 over (0, pi) is pi while the integral of cos^2(nt) is pi/2. The single index n = 0 needs its own constant, so the uniform-looking formula for the normalized system has an exception at the first term. This is the same anomaly as the norm sqrt(2 pi) of u_0 in the trigonometric system of 15.11." .
