<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-affine-line-missing-the-origin> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The set of vectors (x, y, z) in V_3 with 3x + 4y = 1 and z = 0 is a line that does not pass through the origin, so Axiom 5 fails outright: 3(0) + 4(0) = 0, not 1. Axiom 1 fails at the pair (1/3, 0, 0) and (-1, 1, 0), both in the set, whose sum (-2/3, 1, 0) satisfies 3x + 4y = 2; Axiom 2 fails at 2(1/3, 0, 0) = (2/3, 0, 0), which satisfies 3x + 4y = 2. The homogeneous version of the same condition, as in Exercises 22 and 24, is a subspace, so the inhomogeneous right-hand side 1 is the whole defect." .
