<http://studium.local/node/d%3Atriangle-inequality-equality-sufficient-conditions> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Apostol states that equality holds in (d) if x = O, if y = O, or if y = cx for some c > 0, and verifies the last case by the computation ||x + y|| = ||x + cx|| = (1 + c)||x|| = ||x|| + ||cx|| = ||x|| + ||y||. Read the quantifier carefully: these are given as SUFFICIENT conditions only. Unlike the equality clause of Theorem 15.8, this is not an if-and-only-if in the text, and the positivity requirement c > 0 (not merely c nonzero) is what distinguishes it from the dependence condition in Cauchy-Schwarz." .
