<http://studium.local/node/x%3Apythagorean-identity-for-orthogonal-parts> <http://studium.local/p/divergence> "Apostol states it only as a rider to the orthogonal decomposition theorem (15.17), applied to the pair s and s-perp; it is a corollary, not a tool, and he uses it once more inside the proof of the approximation theorem. Strang puts it in position 1 of the section header, before anything else, and immediately reads it off the right triangle b-p-e; for him it is the visual justification of why the perpendicular foot is the closest point. Same identity, opposite pedagogical direction: Apostol derives it from orthogonality and then derives minimality from it algebraically, whereas Strang draws minimality from the picture and uses the identity to confirm it. The consequence is that Strang's version is bound to a right triangle in R^m and does not obviously carry to functions; Apostol's carries with no change of wording." .
