<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atheorem-15-13-orthogonalization-theorem> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "For any finite or infinite sequence x_1, x_2, ... in a Euclidean space V there is a corresponding sequence y_1, y_2, ... in V such that for every k: (a) y_k is orthogonal to every element of L(y_1, ..., y_{k-1}); (b) L(y_1, ..., y_k) = L(x_1, ..., x_k); and (c) the sequence is unique except for scalar factors. Its proof is constructive and by induction, taking y_1 = x_1 and subtracting suitable multiples of the earlier y_i from x_{r+1}." .
