<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atriangle-inequality> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Part (d) of Theorem 15.9: ||x + y|| <= ||x|| + ||y|| for all elements x and y of a Euclidean space. The equality sign holds if x = O, if y = O, or if y = cx for some c > 0. The proof expands ||x + y||^2 and applies the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality." .
<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acomplex-linear-space/anchor/1> <http://studium.local/p/quote> "Although we shall deal primarily with examples of real linear spaces, all the theorems are valid for complex linear spaces as well." .
