<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-increasing-functions-fail-under-negative-scalars> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The set of increasing real-valued functions on the real line, with the usual operations, is closed under addition but not under multiplication by scalars, so Axiom 2 fails: f(x) = x is increasing while (-1)f, that is -x, is decreasing and therefore outside the set. Axiom 6 fails on the same element, because the element (-1)f that Axiom 6 names does not exist in the set at all. The set is closed under multiplication by nonnegative scalars only, which is exactly the defect that separates a convex cone from a linear space." .
