<http://studium.local/node/d%3Atheorem-15-9-holds-for-every-inner-product> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The framing clause of Theorem 15.9: in a Euclidean space, EVERY norm has properties (a)-(d) for ALL elements x and y and ALL scalars c. Combined with the fact that a space may carry several inner products, this is the exact content of the theorem's significance: (a)-(d) are the properties that survive any choice of inner product, and they are therefore the right axioms for a norm in the abstract." .
