<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-parallelogram-law-is-forced-by-an-inner-product> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 16(c) states that ||x + y||^2 + ||x - y||^2 = 2||x||^2 + 2||y||^2 in every Euclidean space, with the cross terms cancelling rather than being estimated. This is a sharper constraint than the triangle inequality: it is an identity, not a bound, and it is exactly what a length function must satisfy to come from an inner product at all. A norm that violates it cannot be written as the square root of any inner product." .
