<http://studium.local/node/d%3Acauchy-schwarz-equality-condition> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The second clause of Theorem 15.8, and the only biconditional in the section: |(x, y)|^2 = (x, x)(y, y) exactly when the set {x, y} is dependent. For nonzero x and y dependence means y = cx, and then the angle between them is 0 if c > 0 and pi if c < 0, so the cosine attains an endpoint of [-1, 1]; if x = O or y = O the set is dependent and equality holds, but the pair has no angle at all under the definition of 15.10. It is here, and only here, that STRICT positivity is required: semi-definiteness would still give the inequality, but with (z, z) = 0 possible for z not O one could have equality without x - ty = O, so dependence could not be concluded." .
