<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-pairing-can-converge-off-the-space> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 13(d) asks for the value of the pairing when x_n = 2^n and y_n = 1/n!, even though the series of squares of 2^n diverges, so this x is not an element of V. The sum of x_n y_n nonetheless converges, to e^2 - 1. Square-summability of both factors is sufficient for convergence but not necessary, so membership in the space and finiteness of the pairing are two separate questions." .
