<http://studium.local/node/d%3A15-10-proof-pair-with-a-single-element> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Pairing each member with x_1 and using (x_1, x_i) = 0 for i not 1 leaves c_1 (x_1, x_1) = 0. Three separate facts are consumed in this one line: additivity, to split the sum inside the inner product; homogeneity, to extract each c_i; and the right-hand side (O, x_1) = 0, itself the c = 0 corollary of homogeneity. Note also that whichever slot x_1 is placed in, one of the two needed rules is NOT an axiom but a consequence of an axiom plus symmetry, since Apostol postulates additivity only in the second slot and homogeneity only in the first." .
