<http://studium.local/node/d%3Ainner-product-additivity-axiom> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Axiom (2): (x, y + z) = (x, y) + (x, z) for all x, y, z. Apostol states additivity in the SECOND slot only; additivity in the first slot is not an axiom but a consequence of (2) together with symmetry. What it forbids: any product that fails to split a sum in its second argument. Dropping only this axiom kills every 'pair the identity with a basis element and expand the sum' argument, i.e. the proofs of Theorem 15.10, Theorem 15.11 and Parseval's formula." .
