<http://studium.local/node/x%3Aindependence-criterion-and-its-consequences> <http://studium.local/p/divergence> "Apostol cashes independence for uniqueness of components (15.08) and, separately, for the extension and exchange results of 15.07; he does not develop it into a battery of equivalent tests. Strang turns it into exactly that: all columns are pivot columns, no free variables, N(A) = {0}, at most one solution of Ax = b, and (in 4.2) A-transpose-A invertible so that x-hat is unique. Every link in that chain is a statement about the *representing matrix*, not about the subspace, which is why Apostol cannot state any of them. The price Strang pays becomes visible only when independence fails: the projection p onto the column space still exists and is still unique, but the coefficient vector x-hat is not -- a distinction that has no counterpart in Apostol, who never separates an element of S from its coefficient tuple." .
