<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-union-of-two-coordinate-planes-fails-additive-closure> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The set of vectors (x, y, z) in V_3 with x = 0 or y = 0 is a union of two planes through the origin and fails Axiom 1: (0, 1, 0) and (1, 0, 0) both belong to the set, but their sum (1, 1, 0) has neither coordinate equal to 0. Axioms 2, 5 and 6 all hold, since the set contains the origin and is closed under every scalar multiple, so this is the case in which closure under addition is the single failing axiom. The inclusive or is what does the damage: replacing it by and gives the z-axis, which is a subspace." .
