<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aorthogonal-set-condition-on-distinct-pairs-only> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Definition: a subset S of V is an orthogonal set if (x, y) = 0 for every pair of DISTINCT elements x and y in S. The word distinct is load-bearing. It exempts the diagonal, so nothing is asserted about (x, x); an orthogonal set may therefore contain the zero element, and its elements are not required to be nonzero. This is precisely the gap that forces the extra hypothesis in Theorem 15.10." .
