<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Atheorem-15-15-orthogonal-decomposition> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Let V be a Euclidean space and S a finite-dimensional subspace. Then every x in V can be written uniquely as x = s + s perp with s in S and s perp in S perp, and the norm of x obeys the Pythagorean formula. Existence is proved by taking a finite orthonormal basis of S and setting s equal to the sum of the projections of x along the basis elements; uniqueness follows because the zero element is the only element orthogonal to itself." .
