<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aparseval-formula-statement> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Equation (15.11): (x, y) = sum over i from 1 to n of (x, e_i) times the conjugate of (y, e_i). It reduces an abstract inner product to a finite sum of scalar products of components, i.e. it says that in an orthonormal basis every Euclidean space computes like V_n with the dot product. Note where the conjugate sits: on the y-factor, i.e. on the component of the SECOND argument." .
