<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aapproximation-inequality-with-equality-only-at-the-projection> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The proof is two steps that discharge the two halves of the claim from a single identity. Step one rewrites x - t = (x - s) + (s - t) and applies the Pythagorean formula, which is licensed because x - s lies in S perp while s - t lies in S; this yields ||x - t||^2 = ||x - s||^2 + ||s - t||^2 and hence the inequality, with no minimization argument anywhere. Step two reads the equality case off the same identity: equality forces ||s - t|| = 0, and it is Theorem 15.9(a),(b) (||z|| = 0 iff z = O) -- not any property of S -- that turns this into t = s." .
