<http://studium.local/node/d%3Atrigonometric-orthogonal-system> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "In the real space C(0, 2pi) with the integral inner product, the functions u_0(x) = 1, u_(2n-1)(x) = cos(nx), u_(2n)(x) = sin(nx) satisfy the integral of u_n u_m over [0, 2pi] equal to 0 whenever m is not n, so S is an orthogonal set. Apostol then draws the independence conclusion in one step: since no member of S is the zero element, S is independent. This is the worked instance of Theorem 15.10, and it shows the nonzero hypothesis being checked by hand rather than assumed." .
<http://studium.local/node/d%3Afunction-space-addition-is-pointwise> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "In every function space of this section the sum f + g is the function whose value at x is f(x) + g(x). Addition of elements is therefore not a new operation at all but addition of real numbers applied at each argument separately." .
