<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-absolute-value-and-product-of-integrals-on-polynomials> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 12 offers two further failures on the space of all real polynomials. Taking the absolute value of the integral of f g preserves symmetry and positivity but destroys homogeneity for negative scalars and additivity. Taking the product of the separate integrals of f and of g is symmetric and bilinear but degenerate, since f(t) = t - 1/2 is nonzero with vanishing integral. The two failures are complementary: the first keeps the sign but loses linearity, the second keeps linearity but loses the sign." .
