<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Alegendre-polynomials> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Applying the orthogonalization theorem to the sequence x_n(t) = t^n in the space of all polynomials with inner product (x, y) = int_{-1}^{1} x(t) y(t) dt yields orthogonal polynomials y_0, y_1, y_2, ...; the Legendre polynomials are their rescalings P_n(t) = ((2n)!/(2^n (n!)^2)) y_n(t) = (1/(2^n n!)) d^n/dt^n (t^2 - 1)^n. The first few are y_0 = 1, y_1 = t, y_2 = t^2 - 1/3." .
