<http://studium.local/node/d%3Aangle-confined-to-the-interval-zero-to-pi> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The definition does not merely solve cos(theta) = (x, y) / (||x|| ||y||); it requires theta to be the solution lying in 0 <= theta <= pi. The interval is part of the stipulation, and it is doing work: over all of R, or even over [0, 2pi], the equation has more than one solution (theta and 2pi - theta share a cosine), so without the restriction the definition would not name a single number. That the restricted equation has exactly one solution is a separate fact, carried by d:angle-well-defined-because-quotient-lies-in-minus-one-to-one." .
