<http://studium.local/node/apostol%3Acx-orthogonality-as-a-minimum-condition> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "Exercise 5 states that (x, y) = 0 if and only if ||x + cy|| >= ||x|| for every real c. This turns orthogonality from an algebraic identity into a minimality statement: y is orthogonal to x exactly when no correction along y shortens x. It is the one-dimensional germ of the Approximation Theorem, where the residual of the best approximation is what is orthogonal to the subspace." .
