<http://studium.local/node/d%3Anormalizing-an-orthogonal-set> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The procedure by which an orthonormal set is manufactured from an orthogonal one: dividing each u_n by its norm gives an orthonormal set with phi_n = u_n / ||u_n||. Two prerequisites are silent. The division requires ||u_n|| nonzero, hence u_n nonzero and hence the positivity axiom; and orthogonality survives the division because scalars pull out of the inner product by homogeneity, so (phi_m, phi_n) is a scalar multiple of (u_m, u_n) and stays zero." .
