<http://studium.local/node/d%3Athm-15-2-same-sum-evaluated-in-two-groupings> <http://studium.local/p/statement> "The proof of Theorem 15.2 assumes two negatives y_1 and y_2 of the same x and then evaluates the single expression y_2 + (x + y_1) twice. Grouped as written it collapses to y_2 because x + y_1 = O; regrouped as (y_2 + x) + y_1 it collapses to y_1 because y_2 + x = O. The two values are values of one expression, so y_1 = y_2." .
